WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:01.107
- Oh my gosh

00:00:01.107 --> 00:00:02.880
- Um, I'm such a fan.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.320
I'm so, have y'all ever met?

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.153
- No.

00:00:05.153 --> 00:00:06.480
- No, but I'm, but I'm in love.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.313
- Only in my dreams.

00:00:07.313 --> 00:00:08.146
- Yeah, exactly.

00:00:08.146 --> 00:00:10.320
- I know y'all both look
really rock and roll right now.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.400
So I'm just loving the vibe

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.600
that you're portraying right now, but...

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.370
- Oh my gosh, we're going
like the best funeral ever.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.145
- We planned it, yeah.

00:00:16.145 --> 00:00:17.400
- The most rock and roll funeral ever.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.830
Um, you started writing
when you were on Glee,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.380
but I heard that nobody really
knew that you were writing.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.790
- No, because I was always really

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.050
kind of secretive about it.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.080
Like I would write, you know,
in sets that weren't being

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.340
used while we were shooting.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.550
And I remember we were doing
this huge obnoxious world tour

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.350
at one point and I would...

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.216
- I really liked it.

00:00:35.216 --> 00:00:36.049
- It was, it was..

00:00:36.049 --> 00:00:36.882
(laughing)

00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:37.715
It was, it was, yeah.

00:00:37.715 --> 00:00:39.540
And I would like, I would
crawl underneath the stage

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.190
and like I would write
like during the show and

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.770
after the show and before
the show and yeah, it was

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.027
it was a crazy time cuz like
we'd, we'd go out, we'd sing

00:00:46.027 --> 00:00:47.910
"Don't Stop Believin'"
and I'd, I'd go, I'd write

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:48.743
down a sentence.

00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:50.220
I'd then go strap on a leotard

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.023
do the single lady dance
and then, then run back out.

00:00:52.023 --> 00:00:54.207
- Just like a normal day that ends in "y".

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.340
- Right, a Tuesday.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.173
- That's cool though.

00:00:57.173 --> 00:00:59.190
I like the idea of creating

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.810
while you're doing something
but it's different.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.480
I love that people are that
creative and can create that.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.313
- Thank you.

00:01:04.313 --> 00:01:05.146
- It's very cool.

00:01:05.146 --> 00:01:05.979
- Thank you so much.

00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:07.620
- This is the 10th anniversary
of the Land of Stories.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.540
So for people who haven't read the books,

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.560
what are they about?

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.170
- So in a nutshell, they're
about a pair of brother

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.090
sister twins named Alex and Connor.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.640
And they inherit a magic
storybook that takes them

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.840
into the fairy tale world.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.970
And over the course of the
series they have adventures

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.740
with all the fairy tale
characters we know and love

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:26.280
and characters from classic
literature and also characters

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.260
in worlds from their own creative writing.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.000
And along the way they
help each other mourn

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.172
the loss of their father.

00:01:31.172 --> 00:01:33.930
And so there's been six
books in the main series

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.300
and I just finished
writing the prequel series

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.475
about their grandparents,
which was three books.

00:01:39.475 --> 00:01:40.308
- I love a prequel.

00:01:40.308 --> 00:01:41.141
- Yeah, and me too.

00:01:41.141 --> 00:01:41.974
It's easy.

00:01:41.974 --> 00:01:43.350
- Yeah. I love a prequel
more than a sequel.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.190
- I do too.

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:45.117
- Yeah.

00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:45.950
- I like, I like figuring out like how

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:46.841
people got where they did.

00:01:46.841 --> 00:01:47.850
- I'm like, wait, we're gonna figure

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.080
out what happened and why it got there.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.700
I think that's so, so clever.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:51.750
- Yeah, it was a lot of fun to write.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:52.830
- Thank you so much.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.750
Like Chris, this is an amazing book.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.610
I just wanted to say that
because it really is cool

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.860
like reading with my kids
and like really enjoying it.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.090
- Oh, I'm, I'm so happy you enjoy it.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:02.733
- It's, it's so good and it's
such an interesting thing

00:02:02.733 --> 00:02:05.100
to go from being loved
as like this character

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.840
and people know you in
a different light to

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.390
know you also have this
whole other talent going on.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:10.980
- Oh, thank you know,
I'm just so fortunate

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.200
that I was I was given
the opportunities to,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.370
to, to do all this stuff.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.900
So I'm, I'm very, very lucky.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.730
- Well, I'm gonna tell you,
I we don't, we can edit this

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.070
out cuz I know we're outta
time, but I actually heard

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.890
of your book whenever I was, I was working

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.200
through like deals like, of
like what I was gonna do.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.400
Cause I wanted to write
children's books, whatever.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.340
And I, and I did, and one
of the companies I met

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.543
with was like, oh my God, there's this

00:02:30.543 --> 00:02:32.250
there's this artist we
love that we've worked

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.083
with and he's actually...

00:02:33.083 --> 00:02:36.330
And they introduced me in
that meeting to your series.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.163
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:37.163 --> 00:02:38.280
- It wasn't even like in a store.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.540
They literally were like, hey

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:40.710
there's this thing you
might be interested.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.870
And I literally read The
Wishing Spell like right then.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.800
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.210
- And I thought it was just so good.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.260
So I just wanted you to say like

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.220
- Please don't cut that out.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.730
- No, I just, no, but I just
wanted, I wanted to tell you

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.710
like your team loves what
you're doing as well.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.880
- Oh thanks, yeah. It's
really great. Thank you.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.000
- Yeah. Well, the 10th anniversary edition

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.400
of The Land of Stories,
The Wishing Spell is out

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.800
now complete with new
illustrations and maps

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.740
which is exciting and everyone
is going home with a copy.

00:03:08.786 --> 00:03:13.200
I love it. And speaking
of putting pen to paper,

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.420
I have some exciting news.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.060
Our season long partner
Pilot Pen is once again

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.870
hosting their $100,000
G2 Overachievers Grant

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.680
and the $15,000 G2
Overachiever Student Grant.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.930
A true overachiever is
someone who goes above

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.420
and beyond their everyday
responsibilities to

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.610
improve their community and the world.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.440
Pilot wants to honor those overachievers

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.040
and give them the recognition
and money they deserve.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.990
Handwritten nominations for both grants

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:43.380
must be submitted by December 31st, 2022.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.630
And next year the finalists
might be featured right here

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:46.710
on the show.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:50.130
We love this, head to g2overachievers.com

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:51.270
to find out how to apply.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.980
Don't miss out on this opportunity.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.043
You have no idea how you
can impact someone's lives.

